# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: sysvar-template-defaults-undocumented -- 18 drawing-dependent sysvars still default to a zero stand-in
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-03

* Observed

The sysvar catalogue (cador/source/sysvar-catalogue.lisp, generated from
autolisp-spec/documentation/system-variables-inventory.sexp) installs a
kind-appropriate ZERO on every cell whose inventory :default is
(:drawing): DIMASZ 0.0, DIMSTYLE "", GRIDUNIT (0 0), CMLSCALE 0.0, ... A
fresh headless drawing therefore looked like no drawing a vendor makes
(found while implementing MLINE, alref Phase 4 S1: CMLSCALE 0 collapses
every multiline onto its path).

* Done (clautolisp 2.2.159, alref Phase 4 S1)

tools/generate-template-defaults.py reads the inventory's documented
"default AutoCAD X (imperial)" (the :divergence text) and generates
cador/source/template-defaults.lisp; populate-default-sysvars installs it
over the stand-ins (full catalogue). 29 of the 47 (:drawing) cells now hold
the acad.dwt value: DIMASZ 0.18, DIMTXT 0.18, DIMSTYLE "Standard", GRIDUNIT
and SNAPUNIT (0.5 0.5), LIMMAX (12 9), TEXTSIZE 0.2, INSUNITS 1,
MEASUREMENT 0, ...

* Remaining

18 cells whose inventory entry states NO imperial value (:divergence NIL
or no "(imperial)" clause), left on the stand-in:

  CIRCULARARROWHEADLENGTH CIRCULARARROWHEADWIDTH CIRCULARARROWLEADERRADIUS
  CIRCULARARROWTHICKNESS CMLSCALE CVIEWDETAILSTYLE DEFAULTSPACEHEIGHT
  DIMDSEP HPNAME INTERIORELEVATIONMINLENGTH INTERIORELEVATIONOFFSET
  LINEARARROWHEADLENGTH LINEARARROWHEADWIDTH LINEARARROWTHICKNESS
  SMDEFAULTTHICKNESS SMEXPORTOSMAPPROXIMATIONACCURACY
  SMEXPORTOSMMINIMALEDGELENGTH UCSNAME

Not filled from memory (AGENTS.md: facts come from the cited vendor pages).
Next: harvest each one's "Initial value" from its AutoCAD 2026 page into
the inventory's :divergence (the generator then picks it up), or measure it
on a fresh imperial drawing. CMLSCALE matters most (MLINE).

* MEASUREMENT (2026-10-04, alref S6)

Both vendors' probe drawings report MEASUREMENT 1 (AutoCAD 2022's
accoreconsole and BricsCAD V26 macOS, sysvar suite, jobs 16916189663 /
16916189664), while cador starts a drawing with 0 (the documented imperial
acad.dwt value). It decides which pattern spacing HATCH uses (metric 3.175
vs imperial 0.125 for ANSI31), so cador's hatches differ from the vendors'
fresh-drawing hatches until this default is settled. Not changed: which
template a "fresh drawing" stands for is pjb's call.

** Decided (pjb 2026-10-04)

"We should initialize MEASUREMENT depending on the locale, if it's not set
explicitly; locale in en_US (LANG, LC_NUMERIC, LC_ALL) would use imperial,
and others would use metric." Done in clautolisp 2.2.169:
populate-default-sysvars sets MEASUREMENT and MEASUREINIT from
LOCALE-MEASUREMENT (first non-empty of LC_ALL, LC_NUMERIC, LANG; en_US ->
0, anything else, unset included -> 1). The other imperial-template values
(DIMASZ 0.18, LIMMAX 12,9, ...) are unchanged: a metric (acadiso.dwt)
fresh drawing would carry metric ones too -- not measured, not done.

* Done (clautolisp 2.2.177, 2026-10-04)

Harvested from the vendor pages (curl of help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2026
"Initial value:" and help.bricsys.com "Default value:", quoted verbatim)
into the inventory's :divergence, then generated:

- All 29 imperial values already installed match AutoCAD 2026; each page
  also states the metric (acadiso.dwt) value, now installed when the
  locale gives MEASUREMENT 1 (*metric-template-defaults*): DIMASZ 2.5,
  DIMSTYLE ISO-25 (an ISO-25 DIMSTYLE record is made so the current style
  names a record), DIMTAD 1, DIMZIN 8, LIMMAX 420,297, INSUNITS 4, ...
- AutoCAD pages: CMLSCALE 1.0000 / 20.0000 (GUID-9E3E86FD-CBF7-4722-BED5-
  17B12709C6F4, now in the inventory), CVIEWDETAILSTYLE Imperial24 /
  Metric50, DIMDSEP . / , , HPNAME ANSI31 / ANGLE (the page says "Saved
  in: Not-saved": a session value MEASUREMENT chooses -- installed with the
  fresh drawing all the same).
- 13 BricsCAD-only cells, from BricsCAD's pages (keyed on INSUNITS 1 / 4,
  which the templates pair with MEASUREMENT 0 / 1): CIRCULARARROW*,
  LINEARARROW*, DEFAULTSPACEHEIGHT, INTERIORELEVATION*, SMDEFAULTTHICKNESS,
  SMEXPORTOSM*.
- UCSNAME: the AutoCAD page states no initial value, only "Returns a null
  string if the current UCS is unnamed"; the stand-in "" is that.
